{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/853193-looting-and-fencing","id":853193,"title":"Looting And Fencing.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-25T15:31:25-07:00","id":853193,"title":"Looting And Fencing.","content":"The Abstract nature of the &quot;Resources background&quot; is, rather blatantly, designed to de emphasize looting, which plays a prominent role in Dungeons and dragons.<br /> <br /> I get the desire for a change of theme, and the emphasis on either trust funds, playing the stock market, or a day job.<br /> <br /> But I find it hard to believe, that when a Garou pack sacks a pentex installation their not going to <br /> loot it<br /> <br /> likewise when some hunters slay a vampire, why not ransack his stuff?<br /> <br /> If your a Nagah, by taking his valuables, you both A: Fund your nest, and B: Potentialy throw hostiles off track, and get them thinking you were a mundane robber who got very very very lucky...<br /> <br /> How difficult should fencing be?<br /> <br /> some jewelry any pawn shop should do<br /> <br /> specialized computers, scanners, like pentex DNA Stark Psychiatric institute or the technocracy have, are best sold, if at all to hard to find speciality markets, <br /> <br /> well thoughts on the idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:47:09-07:00","id":853204,"title":"","content":"You can temporarily raise players resources if they manage to steal some stuff of value, or give them specific items of value (like a car) that they can take. The background tends to represent a long term source of wealth they can draw upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T17:54:26-07:00","id":853251,"title":"","content":"Any ideas on Fencing?<br /> <br /> Contacts is part of it im sure... but finding a buyer for specialized equipment should be difficult<br /> <br /> but the &quot;Armory background&quot; should be available to anyone who wants to invest points on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T18:25:01-07:00","id":853267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/853193-looting-and-fencing?p=853251#post853251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas on Fencing?<br /> <br /> Contacts is part of it im sure... but finding a buyer for specialized equipment should be difficult</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why fences usually have a lot of allies and contacts. Most operate a legitimate business of sorts to sell some of the items they get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  This really shouldn't be this hard to figure out guy 03-25-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T21:00:56-07:00","id":853312,"title":"","content":"For small time deals a pawnshop will work... what kind of legitimate business would the kind of fence a glasswalker who wants to sell some Genetic analysis equpiment they nabbed off DNA, or a vampire who nabbed a sizable collection of military grade fire arms off some hunters (And didnt want to risk stockpiling it) run?<br /> <br /> A valid question I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T02:12:05-07:00","id":853402,"title":"","content":"No one in their right mind would lift equipment that specific unless they had someone lined up that wanted it in the frist place. In which case your not a fence, your a thief.<br /> <br /> Really who goes &quot;yeah, I'll boost that autoclave. I know just the guy&quot; apart from some mysterious persons who might be in the market so they can grow their own designer plague.<br /> <br /> Even then theft of such equipment would be reported to the feds and the news given the horrible implications of what someone would do this making the merchandise hotter then the sun in the eyes of the fence.<br /> <br /> The guns you can sell piece mail out of a cars truck to various street gangs, granted your asking for a lot of heat because no one just sells mil-spec hardware without drawing attention both legal and otherwise. <br /> <br /> In which case your a arms dealer not a fence, however an illegal arms dealer would make a great contact and it's up to them if they want to move a small armory of special forces gear.<br /> <br /> Fences are not some WoW vender you can just dump all your spoils on and they will just pay you top dollar for everything but the kitchen sink. It has to be easy to move (sell) and with little paper trail or legal notice (hotness of item).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Tried to explain as simply as possible with out swearing. 03-26-2016, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T03:17:37-07:00","id":853415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/853193-looting-and-fencing#post853193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">likewise when some hunters slay a vampire, why not ransack his stuff?<br /> <br /> If your a Nagah, by taking his valuables, you both A: Fund your nest, and B: Potentialy throw hostiles off track, and get them thinking you were a mundane robber who got very very very lucky...<br /> <br /> How difficult should fencing be?<br /> <br /> some jewelry any pawn shop should do<br /> <br /> specialized computers, scanners, like pentex DNA Stark Psychiatric institute or the technocracy have, are best sold, if at all to hard to find speciality markets,<br /> <br /> well thoughts on the idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally don't think that the abstraction of wealth is designed to reduce looting anymore than the abstraction of movement and combat is designed to reduce dungeon crawling, its just a favor over narrative terms rather than book keeping or simulation, but...<br /> <br /> Characters can absolutely steal from those that they have fought with or destroyed. Looting is a fine practice in a fantasy game or post apocalyptic setting, there's no social consequences (usually) from taking things through force or violence. Looting in today's world (and in the World of Darkness) is burglary, armed robbery, grand or petty theft, and potentially homicide if your player's characters leave a body behind.<br /> <br /> I think the difference here is the weight of consequences for those kinds of actions bring, particularly if they're something that happens over and over again. Fencing specialized equipment is the type of thing that a fence remembers, and when a group of 'ecoterrorists' are under investigation by Homeland Security (or SAD), and they discover that specialized gene sequencing computers, the type that could make biological weapons, well they might grow concerned. Or if a hunter cell has murdered a witch and steals and sells her valuables, well homicide is going to look into that and the valuables might not be worth very much if they're particularly well known - that makes them harder for a fence to sell. Even without police involvement, word could get out, selling a copy of the Book of Nod or stock bonds worth hundreds of thousands might raise the attention of a dead Vampire's coterie, clan, sect, ghoul(s), or mortal relations. <br /> <br /> At the very least it is painting the picture to whomever the pc's are selling to that they are thieves and possibly murderers (did characters check that expensive rug for blood spatter when they sold it?) which might even set them up to be robbed themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for mechanics, Streetwise represents knowing who to speak to and a certain connection to criminal activity, you might need Wits + Etiquette if they're not familiar with a particular city or scene to establish themselves, if they are established what the characters want for it has to match what's realistic. A shady pawnshop might take any electronics but won't touch firearms, likewise bundles of cash need to get laundered to avoid drawing attention from the IRS or FBI.<br /> <br /> The value is going to always be far less than the retail price for stolen goods because the seller takes on risk if they're caught, items that are traceable are going to be worth less.<br /> <br /> Contacts (criminal) or Perception / Manipulation + Streetwise - locate a fence<br /> Manipulation/ Charisma + Streetwise/ - make a deal<br /> Intelligence + Finance - launder money<br /> Wits + Law/Science - hide evidence<br /> <br /> I would scale the difficulty based on how obscure or 'hot' the things they were trying to fence, and play out a scene anytime it would be enough liquid cash to increase a character's effective resources score. 8 for something difficult to sell like expensive equipment, 9 for anything that would require a specialized buyer like pieces of art or highly valuable goods. Further I'd keep track of how many times the pc's rely on fencing goods, if it was enough to raise a resources dot, I'd make them turn to money laundering or else face the consequences of having an investigation opened on them.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for inspiration the tv shows Better Call Saul and Breaking Bad both deal with criminal processes and the problems that crop up dealing with illegal goods and services.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps, if you're playing a more cinematic kinda game, then I'd say cut it down to a simple roll and reward the characters with a little bit of 'spending money' or a new piece of gear on a success and a minor wrinkle if they don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T07:59:37-07:00","id":853476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/853193-looting-and-fencing#post853193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your a Nagah, by taking his valuables, you both A: Fund your nest, and B: Potentialy throw hostiles off track, and get them thinking you were a mundane robber who got very very very lucky...</div> </div> </div> </div>Lower than bottom tier assassin-judge activity; you'll get a circle tattooed around your heart for things like this, and if there's already one there, it'll get an x over it or a spear through it. Nagah are supposed to make deaths look like a tragic accident that reveals the transgressor's flaws, like having a hidden cannibal Garou choke to death on human flesh, not Killy McLeavestrailsbehind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:52:34-07:00","id":853509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/853193-looting-and-fencing?p=853476#post853476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lower than bottom tier assassin-judge activity; you'll get a circle tattooed around your heart for things like this, and if there's already one there, it'll get an x over it or a spear through it. Nagah are supposed to make deaths look like a tragic accident that reveals the transgressor's flaws, like having a hidden cannibal Garou choke to death on human flesh, not Killy McLeavestrailsbehind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmmn fair point, sure they'd do that if the person was in fact guilty? thought it was called &quot;Punishing the improper strike&quot; for a reason.<br /> <br /> But you have a valid point... any ideas on how they'd handle other indiscretions ones that wont as readily result in a plausible death?<br /> <br /> How do you arrange for a Charach to die in the act?, and for it to look like an accident...<br /> <br /> hmmmn say the only cases the nagah would consider in their juridstiction would probaly involve rape, in which case they'd probaly help the victim, pull the veil of wani out, and shake their head at such a tragic failure of a garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T12:56:58-07:00","id":856666,"title":"","content":"Curious, on Supernaturals looking to sell stuff they've looted, how serioous 